// The two soldier models (soldier2.glb, the player's visible Tripo soldier; operator.glb, the Meshy operator who drives the clips and is the enemy general) are made of
// many separate shells: a closed body, then vest, pouches, straps, helmet parts laid over it. Where a joint bends, shells weighted to the wrong bones slide off or stretch
// like gum, rims lift off the surface they rest on, small holes show the inside. This tool rebuilds both files from their originals (git show <rev>:…), the same way every run:
//   1 drops degenerate / duplicate triangles          2 removes non-manifold fans (hidden or tiny patches hanging off an edge that already has two faces)
//   3 welds cracks (border points closer than K.crack) 4 lays rims on the surface they nearly touch (≤ K.snap)      5 caps small holes (one neighbouring texel: no smear)
//   6 skin weights: gear that slides or tears in the test poses is re-weighted from the body it sits on — the choice that holds closest without stretching (see reweight)
//   7 recomputes normals where it moved or made vertices (hard edges kept)   8 adds a closed low-poly LINER inside torso, arms and legs, parked on one dark texel (same material)
